./ R 00108000          $ 00108010 010                                           
*  ESA/390 SEGMENT TABLE ENTRY. BIT 0 MUST BE ZERO OR EVERY    XA0033DK         
*  TRANSLATION TAKES A SPECIFICATION EXCEPTION -- WHICH IS     XA0033DK         
*  WHAT PRG018 WAS. PTO IS BITS 1-25 WITH SIX ZEROS APPENDED,  XA0033DK         
*  SO PAGE TABLES ARE 64-BYTE ALIGNED. I IS BIT 26, C IS BIT   XA0033DK         
*  27, PTL IS BITS 28-31. RENAMED FROM SEGPAGE WITH NO ALIAS   XA0033DK         
*  SO EVERY SITE MUST BE VISITED. I-121.                       XA0033DK         
SEGPTO   DS    1F             PAGE TABLE ORIGIN, BITS 1-25     XA0033DK         
./ R 00111000          $ 00111010 010                                           
         ORG   SEGPTO+3       THE FLAG BYTE IS BYTE 3 NOW      XA0033DK         
./ R 00112000          $ 00112010 010                                           
*  BITS 24-27 ARE THE TWO LOW PTO BITS PLUS I AND C, SO PTL    XA0033DK         
*  CANNOT LIVE AT BITS 0-3 ANY MORE. THE VALUE IS UNCHANGED    XA0033DK         
*  -- 15 FOR A FULL TABLE -- BECAUSE ESA/390 COUNTS PTL IN     XA0033DK         
*  UNITS OF 16 ENTRIES WHERE S/370 COUNTED PAGES, AND          XA0033DK         
*  256/16-1 IS ALSO 15.                                        XA0033DK         
         DS    BL.4           BITS 24-27: PTO LOW, I, C        XA0033DK         
SEGPTL   DS    BL.4       S*1 BITS 28-31: PAGE TABLE LEN       XA0033DK         
./ R 00114100          $ 00114110 010                                           
* BITS DEFINED IN SEGPTO+3                                     XA0033DK         
./ R 00114200          $ 00114210 010                                           
*  THE ARCHITECTED SEGMENT-INVALID BIT IS 26, NOT 31. X'01'    XA0033DK         
*  WAS INSIDE WHAT IS NOW PTL. RENAMED FROM SEGINV: 14 OF ITS  XA0033DK         
*  31 SITES REACH IT BY DISPLACEMENT OR BY ARITHMETIC ON THE   XA0033DK         
*  VALUE AND NEVER NAME SEGPAGE, SO RENAMING THE CONTAINER     XA0033DK         
*  ALONE WOULD HAVE MISSED THEM.                               XA0033DK         
SEGINVAL EQU   X'20'          SEGMENT INVALID -- BIT 26        XA0033DK         
./ R 00114300          $ 00114310 010                                           
*  SEGMIG IS GONE. IT WAS X'10', WHICH IS THE ESA/390          XA0033DK         
*  COMMON-SEGMENT BIT, AND WHAT-31BIT-NEEDS LISTS THAT         XA0033DK         
*  COLLISION AS UNDESIGNED ITEM 2. IT IS NOT A COLLISION:      XA0033DK         
*  SEGMIG WAS DEFINED HERE AND REFERENCED NOWHERE ELSE IN THE  XA0033DK         
*  TREE. DELETED RATHER THAN MOVED, SO THAT IF ANYTHING EVER   XA0033DK         
*  WANTS IT THE ABSENCE SAYS SO.                               XA0033DK         
*                             (SEGMIG DELETED -- SEE ABOVE)    XA0033DK         
./ R 00114400          $ 00114410 010                                           
*  SEGENQ KEEPS BIT 25, WHICH IS THE LOWEST PTO BIT. THAT IS   XA0033DK         
*  SAFE AND NOT AN OVERSIGHT: IT IS READ ONLY WHEN THE         XA0033DK         
*  POINTER IS ZERO, SO ONLY WITH I SET, AND WITH I SET THE     XA0033DK         
*  HARDWARE DOES NOT INTERPRET PTO AT ALL. PROVED BY           XA0033DK         
*  EXECUTION: X'00000070' IS SEGMENT-INVALID, X'00000050' IS   XA0033DK         
*  A VALID COMMON SEGMENT WITH PTO X'40'.                      XA0033DK         
SEGENQ   EQU   X'40'          ENQUEUED -- ONLY WITH I SET      XA0033DK         
./ R 00139000          $ 00139010 010                                           
*  ESA/390 PAGE TABLE ENTRY -- A FULLWORD, NOT A HALFWORD.     XA0033DK         
*  PFRA IS BITS 1-19, I IS BIT 21, P IS BIT 22, AND BITS 0,    XA0033DK         
*  20 AND 23 MUST BE ZERO. RENAMED FROM PAGCORE WITH NO ALIAS  XA0033DK         
*  BECAUSE 13 LH AND 5 STH SITES WOULD OTHERWISE ASSEMBLE      XA0033DK         
*  CLEAN AND READ THE WRONG TWO BYTES. I-121.                  XA0033DK         
PAGPFRA  DS    1F             PAGE FRAME REAL ADDR, BITS 1-19  XA0033DK         
./ R 00141000          $ 00141010 010                                           
*        BITS DEFINED IN PAGPFRA+2                             XA0033DK         
./ R 00142000          $ 00142010 010                                           
*  PAGE INVALID IS BIT 21, SO X'04' IN BYTE 2. RENAMED FROM    XA0033DK         
*  PAGINVAL: TWO OF ITS SITES REACH IT AS 1(R1) AND NEVER      XA0033DK         
*  NAME THE FIELD.                                             XA0033DK         
PAGINV   EQU   X'04'          PAGE INVALID -- BIT 21           XA0033DK         
./ R 00143000          $ 00143010 010                                           
*  PAGREF KEEPS ITS NAME AND ITS VALUE AND MOVES TO            XA0033DK         
*  PAGPFRA+3, WHICH IS SAFE: BITS 24-31 OF AN ESA/390 PTE ARE  XA0033DK         
*  IGNORED BY THE HARDWARE, SO CP'S PRIVATE FLAG NEEDS NO NEW  XA0033DK         
*  HOME. ALL FOUR SITES NAME PAGPFRA OR PAGINV, SO THEY ARE    XA0033DK         
*  REACHED BY THOSE RENAMES.                                   XA0033DK         
PAGREF   EQU   X'01'          REFERENCED -- AT PAGPFRA+3       XA0033DK         
./ R 00143300 00143400 $ 00143310 010                                           
*  A 1 MB SEGMENT HAS 256 PAGES, NOT 16, AND EACH ENTRY IS     XA0033DK         
*  NOW A FULLWORD, SO A FULL PAGE TABLE IS 16+256*4 = 1040     XA0033DK         
*  BYTES INSTEAD OF 16+16*2 = 48. DERIVED, SO EVERY USER GETS  XA0033DK         
*  THE NEW VALUE -- AND ANY MVC USING IT AS A LENGTH NOW       XA0033DK         
*  EXCEEDS 256 BYTES AND FAILS LOUDLY BY ITSELF.               XA0033DK         
PAGTSWP  EQU   (PAGPFRA-PAGSTMP+256*L'PAGPFRA) LENGTH OF A     XA0033DK         
*                            FULL 256 ENTRY PAGE TABLE         XA0033DK         
./ R 00143500          $ 00143510 010                                           
*  THE SWAP TABLE IS ONE ENTRY PER PAGE TOO, SO IT GROWS 16    XA0033DK         
*  TO 256 WITH THE PAGE TABLE. SWPTABLE IS CP-PRIVATE, SO      XA0033DK         
*  ONLY THE COUNT CHANGES. THE ENTRY SIZE BECOMES ITS OWN EQU  XA0033DK         
*  BECAUSE THE ONE-LINE FORM IS 63 COLUMNS AND A CARD HOLDS    XA0033DK         
*  61 -- THE GENERATOR REFUSED IT RATHER THAN TRUNCATING IT    XA0033DK         
*  INTO THE IDENTIFIER FIELD, WHICH IS WHAT R-04 IS FOR.       XA0033DK         
PAGSWPE  EQU   (SWPCODE-SWPFLAG+1) ONE SWAP ENTRY              XA0033DK         
PAGBMP   EQU   (PAGTSWP+(SWPFLAG-SWPVM)+256*PAGSWPE+8)         XA0033DK         
